      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:f06be5cac919fd62",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run: what did pustaka mean, and what did uppu mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಕಾಲು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಾಲು (kālu) — \"leg, foot\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Proto-Dravidian kāl, and every sister kept it nearly whole: Tamil கால், Telugu కాలు, Malayalam കാൽ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Set that beside ಕೈ, the hand-word, which wore down so far that the family resemblance is hard to see at all. Two body words of the same age; one held its shape and one did not, and nothing about the meaning predicts which."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕಾಲು (kālu) covers the whole limb, foot and leg together. It also names a quarter — a fourth of anything — so ಕಾಲು (kālu) ಗಂಟೆ is a quarter of an hour. Nothing joins the leg to the fraction but an accident of sound, and context is the only fix, which is what context is for."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "DEDR 1479 lists Kannada kāl, \"foot, leg, quarter\", with Tamil kāl and Telugu kālu."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five more body words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
